<article class="project-content" aria-labelledby="atari-project-title">
  <h3 class="project-heading" id="atari-project-title">Atari 2600+ Sideloader</h3>
  <p class="project-lead">A software-only game menu for the Atari 2600+ Pac-Man Edition. Choose games from internal storage with the joystick, while keeping normal cartridge playback.</p>
  <p class="project-compatibility"><strong>Built for:</strong> Pac-Man Edition / firmware 2.0.1.6</p>
  <ul class="technology-list" aria-label="Project technologies"><li>C</li><li>Python</li><li>ARM Linux</li><li>SDL</li><li>Shell</li></ul>
  <figure class="project-figure"><a href={image}><img src={image} alt="The Atari sideloader running on a television, showing a six-game menu with joystick and Fire-button instructions." width="4032" height="2268" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a><figcaption>The game selector running on a Pac-Man Edition console. Up/down to browse, Fire to play.</figcaption></figure>
  <h4>Inside the build</h4>
  <ul class="project-highlights">
    <li><strong>A native console interface.</strong> An ARM game selector written in C reads Linux joystick input and renders through the firmware's existing SDL library.</li>
    <li><strong>Cartridge-first startup.</strong> Booting with an empty slot opens the internal library. Inserting a cartridge before power-on keeps the original playback path.</li>
    <li><strong>Verified updates.</strong> Python tooling checks firmware hashes, backs up the console, writes only the OEM partition, and verifies the full readback against the new image.</li>
  </ul>
  <details class="project-details"><summary>Hardware validation &amp; compatibility</summary><p>The menu, joystick selection, internal Atari 2600 gameplay, and cartridge playback have been reported working on one Pac-Man Edition console. The Atari 7800 game path uses the existing ProSystem core; individual games and controllers still need play checks.</p><p>This release targets Pac-Man Edition firmware 2.0.1.6. The original 2600+ and 7800+ consoles are not supported. See the <a href="https://github.com/Bmanbro/Atari-2600-Sideloader-#compatibility">repository's compatibility notes</a> for details.</p></details>
  <p class="project-credit">Built on work from <a href="https://github.com/MrBlinky/Atari2600plus-loader">MrBlinky's Atari2600plus-loader</a> and Rockchip's rkdeveloptool. Community project, unaffiliated with Atari.</p>
</article>
